{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/505815-hi-my-name-is-tuesday-or-please-help-me-workshop-my-first-vampire","id":505815,"title":"Hi! My name is Tuesday! ( Or; please help me workshop my first vampire)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-06T11:15:40-07:00","id":505815,"title":"Hi! My name is Tuesday! ( Or; please help me workshop my first vampire)","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I come from a primarily changeling the lost background but will be participating in my first VtR session next week. Its going to be set in 1605 london. round about the time of the great gun powder plot and will be a mixture of investigation / politics / slice of unlife. <br /> <br /> Reading through the rules I saw that vampires of a certain blood potency can only feed of the blood of other vampires to gain sustenance... How does that work exactly? do they have a loyal herd of subordinate vamps who willing pimp themselves out as blood dools? (Huh, does the vampires bite cause euphoria for vamp on vamp action?) after all the herd merit gives a flat bonus irrespective of blood potency... How do these vamps avoid the vinculum?<br /> <br /> My character idea is that he was created by a Marquis DeSade type vampire. Originally the marquis just kept a herd of humans in his oubliettes but as his blood potency raised he turned those blood dolls into vampires in order to maintain his supply. Literally my character was his tuesday meal. then of course things went horribly wrong, either the marquis died or went into torpor or fled or lost interest (I Havant decided) and tuesday was free from his master. I see Tuesday as a Incredibly naive, socially awkward but very chipper and really just super jazzed about this whole world thing that exists outside of his old cell. <br /> <br /> Im thinking he probably grew up being a blood doll and was turned in his early twenties, maybe hed never even seen the sun before he was turned. knew nothing of the rules or nature of vampire life. Maybe even walked out into the sun on that first day (a painful lesson)<br /> <br /> This all feels very europian, so I figure maybe the holy roman empire, some distant provance... and he made his way to london.... somehow? <br /> <br /> I dont know what function he provides in vampire?<br /> What skills can I actually give him?<br /> how do vampires who need to feed on other vamps avoid vinculum?<br /> Are there any hideous flaws in this idea?<br /> <br /> Thanks so very much for any help in advance!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:26:04-07:00","id":505864,"title":"","content":"I had a demon named Wednesday.<br /> <br /> This is not relevant, just curious.<br /> <br /> Vampires that are required to eat vampires do not suffer from Viniculum.<br /> <br /> THe question of function is probably one he'll have to explore in game. More important is if he decides his own function, or if he can define it for himself before anyone else does.<br /> <br /> You can probably give him high social just for interacting with other inmates. Since you want him to be naive, probably keep the mental low, so give him some Physical as his secondary.<br /> <br /> Thing of the matter is that Vampires rarely have blood dolls just for the sake of feeding, since that's incriminating as hell and also a waste of resources. He probably cultivates them into staff of various sorts, granting that most of them are house staff of a sort-keep the grounds, do the laundry, lie with him when he wants to pretend to humanity, etc. That's more entertaining and believable, and gives you more room to move around.<br /> <br /> Barring the &quot;Vampires who need to eat vampires don't suffer Viniculum&quot; thing, there are rituals and scales that also approach covering Viniculum, if you feel they must have a defense.<br /> <br /> Are there any hideous flaws in this idea? Just the limits of the cage. Why have a buffet when you can have a cleaning crew <i>and</i> a buffet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:32:16-07:00","id":505875,"title":"","content":"Wait, are we talking first or second edition here? <br /> <br /> Because if it's second edition elders are immune to blood <i>addiction. </i>Vinculum just gets a resistance roll. One that gets weaker every time you use it on the same vamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:33:53-07:00","id":505879,"title":"","content":"Oh, those aren't the same?<br /> <br /> Quick notice: If someone says something that contradicts what I say in Vampire affairs, listen to them. Vampire is not my strong suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:40:16-07:00","id":505883,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the addiction to Vitae and the Vinculum are two different things that can happen as a consequence of consuming Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T11:43:26-07:00","id":505885,"title":"","content":"One sure-fire way to avoid getting bonded to a vampire you feed from regularly: Get yourself bonded to someone <i>else. </i>You can only have one full blood bond at a time. Failing that an elder could go 2 way with a younger kindred they use as a dedicated filter. It's frowned upon, but a guy based on the Marquis de Sade getting into something known as Perversion sounds quite fitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T12:50:41-07:00","id":505984,"title":"","content":"&quot; Mister Wednesday. Although given the weather, it might as well be Thursday &quot; - Mr Wednesday, American Gods. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We will be playing first edition as my GM is a little flighty about second edition (give him time)<br /> <br /> So, perhaps Tuesday was required to provide other services, akin to a harem or concubine? Perhaps Friday was harp, Tuesday way poetry and Wednesday was a good hard shag. I like this idea, part of the characters naivete is that the only source of education he had were the greek plays he was forced to memorries and recount. He sees the world through the epics of antiquity, homer, etc. It also gives him an excuse to have some education and the ability to read.<br /> <br /> Hm.... Les Gens Libres, Kallisti and the Neglatu bloodlines cant form the vinculum. I don't know if that means both ways or just when being drunk upon. I suppose his maker could have been one of those bloodlines to be honest as its backstory it can be glossed over slightly. <br /> <br /> Ill put points into latin, greek, acadmeics ....<br /> <br /> hmm....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T06:41:34-07:00","id":506707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/505815-hi-my-name-is-tuesday-or-please-help-me-workshop-my-first-vampire#post505815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading through the rules I saw that vampires of a certain blood potency can only feed of the blood of other vampires to gain sustenance... How does that work exactly? do they have a loyal herd of subordinate vamps who willing pimp themselves out as blood dools? (Huh, does the vampires bite cause euphoria for vamp on vamp action?) after all the herd merit gives a flat bonus irrespective of blood potency... How do these vamps avoid the vinculum?</div> </div> </div> </div>You dont have to worry about this until you are blood Potency 6, but I am thinking this is for your Sire, not your character? You can also take a few merits to help avoid feeding on vampires. They could have a personal herd of Blood Bonded vampires, understanding friends, or whatever really. That's up to you and the story teller to work out. However you will likely get the Viniculum/Bond with your food, double edge sword there. Yes the Kiss if done nonviolently is a wonderful thing for humans and vamps alike, however just not mechanically so for vamps, unless you spend a will power. Other than just not feeding off vampires, there really isnt much in the way to avoid the Bond. There are some merits, your blood potency helps resist it, i think there is a coil too?? not sure on that. You will inevitably get addicted to Vitae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nurseninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/505815-hi-my-name-is-tuesday-or-please-help-me-workshop-my-first-vampire#post505815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont know what function he provides in vampire?<br /> What skills can I actually give him?<br /> how do vampires who need to feed on other vamps avoid vinculum?<br /> Are there any hideous flaws in this idea?<br /> <br /> Thanks so very much for any help in advance!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would give something along the lines of Academics as you have mentioned. Medicine because you likely would have had to take care of yourself a lot, maybe the other dolls too. Empathy, Survival. Athletics? - Just suggestions of course. Survival to take care of yourself. Athletics because maybe you worked out in your cell because you were bored. Empathy because you could relate and got to know your fellow Dolls?<br /> <br /> Merits Language and Multilingual are great for what you were going for. Perhaps Area of Expertise in to a specialty for Academics (Epics ) Striking looks never hurts.<br /> <br /> Your function as a vampire is up to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think this is a great concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:10:20-07:00","id":507207,"title":"","content":"&quot;My master... sire as I now know is the correct word, he had great difficulty with Mondays. They never lasted more than a few seasons. I confess I know not what memory or daemon troubled him about that particular day or exactly what happened in that room but when the mood was upon him... we could hear the screams. the Mondays, they died poorly. The rest of us grew up within the confines of the marquis winter palace. but the Mondays? the marquis imported those poor souls&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Did I tell your it was a Monday who told me about London? The last Monday I mean, the summer Monday. He talked about the fish markets, the bars, the shit filled streets... it sounded... magical. see, I only knew of sparta and Socrates, wine and Medusa's... Id never heard of harpzicords or cards and gambling. After the fire, after everyone scattered to the winds... London<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wait.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Are Medusa's even real?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","user":"Nurseninja","date":". 05-07-2015, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4190-nurseninja","name":"Nurseninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}